  "narrative": "Iteration 2 explore focuses on three scientific needs: context-specific robustness of the already accepted strong dependency associations, resolution of borderline MAPK driver claims after the initial broad tests, and a small expansion into biologically motivated DNA-repair/chromatin contexts. First, I register main-effect refinements for the accepted strong effects within adenocarcinoma: SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA2 dependency, TP53 wild-type versus TP53-loss for USP7 dependency, KEAP1-loss versus weaker NFE2L2 dependency under the reversed direction, and MSI-high versus WRN dependency. These are absolute subgroup effect checks rather than interaction tests; they are useful because a large accepted effect could be diluted, concentrated, or absent in the largest lineage subtype. Second, I register pure-context refinements for MAPK dependencies. The broad KRAS and ERBB2 effects remain unresolved, and the broad BRAF test was negative. Excluding alternative MAPK pathway drivers may reveal a cleaner oncogene-selective effect if the prior nulls were diluted by mixed driver biology. This remains hypothesis generation in the supplied dataset, not a causal test. Third, I add an ARID1A-loss versus SMARCA2 dependency test restricted to SMARCA4-intact cells, which asks whether a second BAF subunit loss marks SMARCA2 dependency independently of the canonical SMARCA4-loss context. Finally, I add a technical robustness check for SMARCA4-loss versus SMARCA2 dependency within the dominant Avana library and a biologically motivated WRN context using BRCA2 loss. These proposals are registered as unresolved because they are new comparisons. Direction coding follows the established convention: direction -1 means a positive signed estimate corresponds to a more negative dependency score in the exposed group, while direction +1 means a positive signed estimate corresponds to a less negative/stronger raw score in the exposed group. For NFE2L2, the reversed accepted finding used direction +1 because KEAP1 loss appeared to weaken dependency, so subtype-robustness claims keep that sign.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 2 exploration plan: analyze priority should first cover H14-H23 pending context and untested outcome claims, then new H24-H33 if slots remain. Highest-value new claims: accepted-effect robustness in adenocarcinoma H24-H27, pure-context MAPK refinements H28-H30, ARID1A-SMARCA2 independent context H31, Avana-library robustness for SMARCA2 H32, and BRCA2-WRN H33. If any subgroup or eligibility-restricted comparison fails the 20-cell rule, prefer the corresponding broad main effect or a broader binary subgroup rather than forcing a tiny cell. Accepted main dataset findings remain H6 SMARCA4 loss/SMARCA2, H7 MSI-high/WRN, H12 TP53 wild-type/USP7, and H13 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2. Unresolved main effects remain H1 KRAS, H4 ERBB2, H5 MDM2; H3 EGFR rejected after validation; H2, H8-H11 rejected. Keep validation reserved for precise effects crossing relative 10% benchmark and biological/technical coherence, especially subtype or library robustness of accepted large effects."
